From 20926bf68d71fc8c566dcdeb4319fb72d0cf64be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pete Schwamb <pete@schwamb.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:16:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Talk to a simulated pod when the Simulator has Bluetooth

In the Simulator, pod commands were always mocked. With ImpossiBLE
injected (serving LoopKit/pod), a DASH or Omnipod 5 pod has a real
Bluetooth path, so pairing, priming, cannula insertion, time changes,
deactivation, beeps and silencing now go to it. Without ImpossiBLE, and
for Eros pods, which need a RileyLink, the mocks run as before.

The check matches G7SensorKit's: ImpossiBLE's CBSPeripheral class is
present.

(cherry picked from commit e60e0abae71f1cb5627c4b7011620a10edf6b1c7)
(cherry picked from commit 868599d8ad7fb353e5abf030e16e05387502a95d)
